/** @page api_installed Installed C++ interfaces

The four project headers under `include/gige_mel/` are installed by
`GigeMelProvider`. Start with @ref md_docs_2consumer-integration "Integrating a MEL Consumer"
for installation and capture, then see @ref md_docs_2architecture "architecture"
and the @ref md_docs_2implementation-profile "MEL implementation profile".

Ordinary native MEL consumers use the pinned upstream factory declarations and
channels; this reference does not regenerate the upstream MEL API. The installed
project C++ backend contract is a **source-level integration contract, not a
stable cross-toolchain plugin ABI**. The upstream factory lookup symbols have C
linkage but use C++ types and are not a C API.

Header | Entry points
------ | ------------
@ref include/gige_mel/provider.hpp "provider.hpp" | @ref gige_mel::make_api_manager, @ref gige_mel::ProviderSettings, @ref gige_mel::ProviderStatistics and @ref gige_mel::provider_statistics
@ref include/gige_mel/backend.hpp "backend.hpp" | @ref gige_mel::backend::ICameraBackend, @ref gige_mel::backend::ICameraDevice, @ref gige_mel::backend::IFrameStream, @ref gige_mel::backend::FrameLease, @ref gige_mel::backend::FrameDescriptor, @ref gige_mel::backend::CameraConfiguration and @ref gige_mel::backend::CameraCapabilities
@ref include/gige_mel/navigation.hpp "navigation.hpp" | @ref gige_mel::backend::NavigationReport and optional @ref gige_mel::backend::INavigationSink
@ref include/gige_mel/line_of_sight.hpp "line_of_sight.hpp" | @ref gige_mel::backend::LosSupport and @ref gige_mel::backend::LosObservation

## Optional source capabilities

- LOS: @ref gige_mel::backend::ILineOfSightSource and
  @ref gige_mel::backend::ILineOfSightStream.
- Stacked images: @ref gige_mel::backend::IStackedImageSource,
  @ref gige_mel::backend::IStackedImageStream, @ref gige_mel::backend::StackSupport,
  and @ref gige_mel::backend::StackLease.

The presence of a C++ interface is not a guarantee that a source supports the
capability; see @ref md_docs_2status "current capability and evidence status".
*/